On Fri, 5 Jul 2002, Carsten Grohmann wrote:

> I have some SuSE specific rules. It is possible to open a contribution branch
> add this and other rules to the SELinux package?

It might be best to use the sourceforge selinux project site for such
contributions.  You might create a contrib/suse tree in the CVS repository
there.  Create an account at sourceforge and then send email to Howard
Holm or Mark Westerman asking them to add you as a developer to the
project.

